### Admin Portal

#### [NEW] [AdminLayout.jsx](file:///d:/Project/Other%20projects/Ganesh/Fish_commerce/src/pages/admin/AdminLayout.jsx)
- Route guard — redirects non-admin users
- Top bar with "Admin Dashboard" title, notification bell with pending order count
- Tab navigation: Product Management | Pending Orders | Order History
- `<Outlet />` for nested admin routes

#### [NEW] [AdminProducts.jsx](file:///d:/Project/Other%20projects/Ganesh/Fish_commerce/src/pages/admin/AdminProducts.jsx)
- Product table with columns: Image, Name, Price, Stock, Care Level, Status, Actions
- Actions: Edit (opens modal), Toggle Availability, Delete (with confirm)
- "Add New Fish" button → opens modal with full form (name, price, image URL, care dropdowns, stock, description)
- "Publish Product" saves via ProductContext

#### [NEW] [AdminOrders.jsx](file:///d:/Project/Other%20projects/Ganesh/Fish_commerce/src/pages/admin/AdminOrders.jsx)
- Tab sub-filter: Pending | History (Confirmed/Shipped/Delivered)
- Table columns: Order ID, Customer Name, Phone & Email, Fish Ordered, Delivery Address, Date, Status, Actions
- Status workflow buttons: Mark as Confirmed → Shipped → Delivered
- Toast notification on status change

---

### App Shell & Routing

#### [NEW] [App.jsx](file:///d:/Project/Other%20projects/Ganesh/Fish_commerce/src/App.jsx)
- Wraps all context providers
- React Router with routes:
  - `/` → Home
  - `/products` → Catalog
  - `/products/:id` → ProductDetail
  - `/checkout` → Checkout
  - `/order-success` → OrderSuccess
  - `/auth` → Auth
  - `/admin` → AdminLayout (guarded)
    - `/admin/products` → AdminProducts
    - `/admin/orders` → AdminOrders

#### [NEW] [main.jsx](file:///d:/Project/Other%20projects/Ganesh/Fish_commerce/src/main.jsx)
- Mounts `<App />` into `#root`

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Online payment required** — checkout uses Razorpay and creates an order only after server-side payment verification.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Admin access** — hardcoded admin login: `admin@fishcommerce.com` / `admin123`. Any other credentials log in as a regular user.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **No real backend** — all data is stored in localStorage. Product seed data is loaded on first visit. This means data is per-browser and resets if localStorage is cleared.

> [!WARNING]
> **Fish images** — I will generate a few key images (hero Betta fish, some product photos) using the image generation tool and use placeholder URLs for the remainder. You can replace them with real photos later.

---

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- No unit test framework is being set up in this initial build (no existing tests in the empty workspace).
- Verification will be done via browser-based flow testing.

### Browser Flow Testing
I will use the browser subagent tool to verify the following end-to-end flows:

1. **Homepage renders** — Navigate to `http://localhost:5173/`, confirm hero text, CTAs, and animated tank card are visible.
2. **Catalog browsing** — Click "Explore Catalog", verify product grid loads with all fish cards. Test filter pills (Freshwater, Beginner) and search.
3. **Product detail** — Click a product card, verify detail page shows image, specs box, price, "Adopt / Order Now" button.
4. **Cart flow** — Add item to cart, verify cart count updates in navbar. Navigate to checkout.
5. **Auth gate** — On checkout, verify guest/login prompt appears. Test login with test credentials.
6. **Order placement** — Fill checkout form, submit order, verify redirect to `/order-success` with order reference.
7. **Admin login** — Log in as `admin@fishcommerce.com` / `admin123`, navigate to `/admin`.
8. **Admin product CRUD** — Add a new fish product, verify it appears in the admin table and in the customer catalog.
9. **Admin order management** — Verify the order placed earlier appears in Pending Orders. Click "Mark as Confirmed", verify status updates.

### Manual Verification (User)
- Review visual design against the color palette and typography spec
- Test on mobile viewport (resize browser to ~375px width)
- Verify all navigation links work correctly
